Following our call, this confirms the staff's understanding of Marchwood Ca=
pital Partners LP (SEC File No. 801-71204) and its Form PF obligations.<br =
/>
<br />
Based on the regulatory assets under management attributable to private fun=
ds that you reported to us, Marchwood Capital is a smaller private fund adv=
iser and will file Form PF annually rather than quarterly. Your first annua=
l filing will cover the fiscal year ending December 31, 2012 and is due wit=
hin 120 days of that date.<br />
<br />
You asked which funds must be aggregated. Aggregation applies to parallel f=
und structures and to master-feeder arrangements as described in the Form P=
F instructions, and to funds advised by your related persons unless those r=
elated persons report separately. On the facts you described, the two feede=
rs into the Marchwood Diversified Master Fund are aggregated with the maste=
r and reported as a single fund.<br />
<br />
This is staff guidance on the reporting form only. It is not a determinatio=
n about the status of any fund under the Advisers Act.<br />
